<title>CANADA: Canada government cash balances fall in week.</title>
<headline>Canada government cash balances fall in week.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The government of Canada's cash balances rose in the week that ended February 26, the Bank of Canada said on Friday.</p>
<p>				     Wk to Feb 12 Chg on wk Chg on yr</p>
<p>Notes in circulation		  26.67   +0.138    +0.668</p>
<p>Government cash balances	     4.63   -2.167    +0.879</p>
<p>Govt securities outstanding	461.76   -0.156    +7.162</p>
<p>Treasury bills			 128.80   -0.100   -29.900</p>
<p>Canada savings bonds		  33.07   -0.055    +2.095</p>
<p>All figures in billions of dollars.  </p>
<p>					   Jan 97     Dec 96     Jan 96</p>
<p>M1					  68.53	69.74	59.96</p>
<p>M2					 395.28     398.32     388.67</p>
<p>M3					 498.28     500.53     472.55</p>
<p>Note - Figures are unadjusted, in billions of dollars.</p>
<p>   Chartered bank assets			 Jan	   Dec</p>
<p>   Net foreign currency			-16.27	-13.93</p>
<p>   Canadian dollar			     685.02	685.04</p>
<p>   Total Canadian liquid assets	    105.33	108.04</p>
<p>((Reuters Ottawa Bureau (613) 235-6745))</p>
</text>
